  "id": "oligodendrocyte",
  "term": "oligodendrocyte",
  "definition": "An oligodendrocyte is a type of glial cell that forms the myelin sheath around axons. It also matures during brain development and can take part in remyelination in adulthood; problems in these processes have been linked to cognitive and behavioral dysfunction and to disorders such as schizophrenia.",
